<!--
  Only the genuinely public pages are listed.

  The application is a single-page app, so every private path returns the same
  shell and has nothing of its own to index; those are disallowed in robots.txt
  and marked `noindex, nofollow` at runtime by src/seo/RouteMeta.jsx.

  The /guides and /personal-trainer-software URLs are NOT part of that SPA.
  They are static HTML generated by scripts/generate-content-pages.mjs and
  served straight off disk, so they carry their content in the response body
  rather than depending on a crawler executing JavaScript.

  `lastmod` is maintained by hand. There are nine URLs, so a generator would be
  more machinery than the problem deserves — but it does mean the dates go stale
  silently. Update them when the page content actually changes, and only then:
  a lastmod that moves on every deploy teaches Google to ignore it.
-->
